# =============================================================================
# EOL shield — normalise all text to LF in the working tree (windows #46 class)
# =============================================================================
# Rationale (estate hygiene campaign, 2026-09-25; mirrors the phlix-windows-client
# PR #46 precedent and the tizen/ui/contracts/hub/roku shields):
#
# If any windows-latest CI job ever lands on this repo, git's autocrlf line
# endings (or a machine-level core.autocrlf=true) can silently convert
# working-tree text files to CRLF at checkout. Three byte laws are exposed:
#
#  1. tests/fixtures/server-route-manifest.json is vendored byte-for-byte from
#     @phlix/contracts dist/server-route-manifest.json and HARD-PINNED by md5 in
#     tests/Unit/Api/ServerRouteManifestGateTest.php (EXPECTED_MD5
#     06ce7ec95bc064cc0f13b94389af9a82 — gate s405-console-route-gate-v1).
#  2. build/phlix.phar is a COMMITTED distribution artifact (mode 755) executed
#     by tests/PharTest.php — any line-ending munging of the zip container or
#     its stub bytes corrupts the shipped binary outright.
#  3. docs/images/ terminal-capability references (png/gif) are committed
#     rendering evidence.
#
# `* text=auto eol=lf` forces LF working-tree bytes on every text file on
# every platform regardless of core.autocrlf; git detects text vs binary by
# content (NUL heuristic), so binary files never convert. Committed blobs are
# already pure LF (2026-09-25 census @4ea13bed: 754 tracked blobs, CR only in
# png/gif/phar assets — all guarded below), so renormalisation is a guaranteed
# no-op and this file only FROZE the invariant against future checkouts.
# vendor/ (composer-managed, untracked) is unaffected.
# =============================================================================
* text=auto eol=lf
# Committed binary artifacts and rendering evidence: never EOL-converted.
*.png binary
*.gif binary
*.phar binary
